  "description": "The ideal bike for those seeking a versatile, agile and comfortable that's as capable on the tarmac as it is on the trail, meet the Ragley Trig. Suited to bikepacking adventures, inner-city commutes, rapid off-road trail riding and everything else in-between, the Trig is a reliable choice for any venture. Plus, it features a full Chromoly (CrMo) frame, Ragley Carbon forks, a Shimano GRX 1x11-Speed groupset and hydraulic disc brakes. And, it rolls fast and stable upon Nukeproof Neutron hubs, WTB ST i25 Tubeless Ready rims and WTB Sendero 650bx47c Tubeless tyres.\nThe Trig has been a firm favourite for a massively diverse group of riders. We have seen them fully loaded for multi-day adventures, shod with slicks as an urban commuter, or just ridden stock for local lockdown sanity missions.\n700c and 650b Compatible with Wide Tyre Clearance\nThe Trig frameset features a 44mm headtube, multiple bottle cage mounts and tyre clearance to run any 700 or 650 gravel tyre option you want (and up 2.1” wide MTB tyres on 27.5” wheels). Want to get a little rowdier with your drop-bar endeavours? It’s even dropper post compatible for future off-road biased upgrades.\nLightweight and Supple Chromoly Steel Frame with 12mm Thru-Axles\nThe frame is engineered from custom triple-butted 4130 Chromoly steel tubing resulting in a frame that is lightweight and supple enough to provide comfort on longer trail rides whilst robust and stiff enough to take some serious abuse. The carbon fork features a 12mm thru-axle and the mounting points you need to take to the backcountry.\nWe’re not going to pigeonhole the Trig as gravel or adventure anymore. It’s all the same thing. We just made a super fun and reliable bike for you to go find your own adventure.",
